<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 64,849 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 64,849 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 64,849 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday, compared to 36,978 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Wednesday	Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 7,961	    7,783</p>
<p>    Import cargo			56,888	   29,195</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, six ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours four ships were expected to sail and eight were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		  Berthing</p>
<p>Feul oil		 40,000	 Al Safa	     1/10</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Wawasan Megah     3/10</p>
<p>High speed deisel    55,000	 Al Maqwa	     due</p>
<p>Sugar		    13,000	 Halldor	     1/10</p>
<p>High speed deisel    56,000	 Kanpolis	    8/10</p>
<p>Sugar		    12,000	 Gur Maiden	   due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
